    'ar.role':             'Project Developer &middot; ArtReal AG',
    'ar.both-kicker':      'Back to the plan.',
    'ar.both-title':       'With everything in between.',
    'ar.both-l-label':     'What I bring from construction',
    'ar.both-l-text':      'An apprenticeship as a qualified architectural draftswoman, years in a planning office and project management of architecture projects. I read a plan before anyone explains it.',
    'ar.both-r-label':     'What I have learned since',
    'ar.both-r-text':      'Leading projects with many stakeholders, tight deadlines and full budget responsibility &ndash; and presenting them so that others say yes.',
    'ar.salutation':       'Dear ArtReal AG team',
    'ar.p1':               'I started at the drawing board: four years of apprenticeship as a qualified architectural draftswoman, then more years in a planning office and finally as project manager at Architektur H&uuml;rzeler AG in Erlenbach. There I led architecture projects, communicated with clients and presented projects visually. With this application I want to return to real estate &ndash; as a project developer.',
    'ar.p2':               'Since 2023 I have worked in live marketing. At TIT-PIT I lead Migros&rsquo;s presence at more than ten big Swiss festivals, with full budget responsibility. That sounds far from construction, but it isn&rsquo;t: I coordinate permits, authorities, suppliers and build crews, plan spaces to scale and make sure everything is standing on the day. A festival site is a construction site with a fixed opening date.',
    'ar.p3':               'ArtReal draws me because you accompany projects from the first sketch to handover &ndash; development, general planning and construction management from a single source. Projects like the H&auml;fliger Areal in Wettingen show what matters to me: housing that is well thought out, built sustainably and easy to market. In development I can use both things I bring: an understanding of planning and construction, and experience in selling and steering projects.',
    'ar.p4':               'I don&rsquo;t have a degree in real estate economics, but a rare combination: I understand a plan, I can lead a project, and I know how to present it. I am ready to get up to speed quickly on feasibility, returns and building law.',
    'ar.closing':          'I look forward to telling you the rest in person.<br>Kind regards<br>Shayna Jucker',
    'ar.day-heading':      'from plot to handover',
    'ar.day-sub':          'How I approach a development project',
    'ar.d1-time':          '01',
    'ar.d1-label':         'Assess the plot',
    'ar.d1-text':          'Understand location, zoning, permitted density and surroundings. What is possible on this plot &ndash; and what makes sense?',
    'ar.d2-time':          '02',
    'ar.d2-label':         'Clarify feasibility',
    'ar.d2-text':          'Sketch first volumes and variants, estimate costs roughly and compare them with returns before much money goes into planning.',
    'ar.d3-time':          '03',
    'ar.d3-label':         'Define the project',
    'ar.d3-text':          'Set the unit mix, standard and sustainability goals &ndash; together with planning, the client and marketing.',
    'ar.d4-time':          '04',
    'ar.d4-label':         'Accompany the permit',
    'ar.d4-text':          'Prepare the building application, communicate with authorities and neighbours and follow up open points until the permit is granted.',
    'ar.d5-time':          '05',
    'ar.d5-label':         'Steer delivery',
    'ar.d5-text':          'Keep costs, deadlines and quality in view. Every open item has a name and a date.',
    'ar.d6-time':          '06',
    'ar.d6-label':         'Market and hand over',
    'ar.d6-text':          'Design visualisations, documents and website so tenants and buyers can picture their home &ndash; right up to the key handover.',
    'ar.work-heading':     'work',
    'ar.work-sub':         'From my time in architecture',
    'ar.work-p1':          'In my portfolio I show architecture projects and plans from my apprenticeship and my time in the planning office &ndash; floor plans, sections, elevations and visualisations.',
    'ar.work-btn1':        'View architecture',
    'ar.work-btn2':        'View plans',
    'ar.match-sub':        'What I bring to the role',
    'ar.m1-label':         'Understanding planning and construction',
    'ar.m1-text':          'Qualified architectural draftswoman and years in a planning office: floor plans, sections, details, building applications. I speak the language of architects and contractors.',
    'ar.m2-label':         'Leading projects',
    'ar.m2-text':          'Project management of architecture projects at Architektur H&uuml;rzeler AG and today of more than twenty live dates a year &ndash; from briefing to close.',
    'ar.m3-label':         'Owning budgets',
    'ar.m3-text':          'Full budget responsibility for large client projects. I go into budget talks with variants and clear numbers, not an opinion.',
    'ar.m4-label':         'Leading many stakeholders',
    'ar.m4-text':          'Clients, authorities, suppliers, build crews: I am used to information coming together with me and decisions not being left lying.',
    'ar.m5-label':         'Accompanying clients',
    'ar.m5-text':          'Client communication was already my part of the work in the architecture office. I explain a project so that non-experts understand it too.',
    'ar.m6-label':         'Presenting and marketing',
    'ar.m6-text':          'Visualisation, graphics, photography and copy I do myself. I can create project documents and marketing material without an agency.',
    'ar.m7-label':         'Software',
    'ar.m7-text':          'ArchiCAD, Vectorworks and 3D visualisation from architecture, plus Adobe Creative Cloud, Figma and Microsoft Office.',
    'ar.m8-label':         'German and English',
    'ar.m8-text':          'Both native. I write documents for investors or international partners at publication level.',
    'ar.fact1':            'Available from November 2026',
    'ar.fact2':            'Based in Pf&auml;ffikon ZH &ndash; about 25 minutes to Wallisellen',
    'ar.fact3':            'German and English native &ndash; French and Italian not at working level',
    'ar.fact4':            'No degree in real estate economics and not in the construction industry since 2023 &ndash; but an apprenticeship, a planning office and project management in architecture',
    'ar.fact5':            'Qualified architectural draftswoman, vocational baccalaureate in design',
    'ar.fact6':            'BSc Multimedia Production FHGR, specialisation Live Communication, exchange semester in the Netherlands',
    'ar.fact7':            'Speculative application: I am applying as a project developer, even if no position is advertised right now',
    'ar.skills-sub':       'Architecture &middot; Management &middot; Design &middot; Tools &middot; Marketing',
